  "economy": {
    "canonical_prices": [],
    "price_claims": [
      {
        "text": "Star Lord Wan Xiang sells star dart Gu with other star path mortal Gu such as stellar fire Gu, falling meteor Gu, and star river Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          666
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "immortal-market-and-killer-move-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The offensive killer move spiral drill star spear needs small numbers of Spiral Bone Spear Gu, several star river Gu, countless star dart Gu, and large numbers of shooting star Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          667
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "immortal-market-and-killer-move-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_spiral_bone_spear_gu",
          "gu_shooting_star_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Star dart Gu is a rank one mortal Gu transformed from ordinary insects, unlike starlight firefly Gu production. Any insect that enters deep sleep inside a star cave rock filled with surface holes can change after forty-nine days; a portion of those slumbering insects become star dart Gu. Beyond that insect origin and the dart-shaped fossil, no living appearance is given.",
        "chapters": [
          851
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production-and-later-trade",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Its food is the bamboo juice of the arrow bamboo forest. In Star Lord Wan Xiang’s blessed land, that forest sits over star cave rocks, and past bamboo juice once formed a thick blue fog that was a top quality place to raise the Gu. Fang Yuan judges that the forest needs moon well water to restore that habitat.",
        "chapters": [
          851
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production-and-later-trade",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Star Lord Wan Xiang mainly sold star dart Gu with his other star path mortal Gu, and ordinary lots such as star dart Gu were sold in bulk on a competitive market.",
        "chapters": [
          851
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production-and-later-trade",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After Fang Yuan takes over that blessed land, later chapters still list star dart Gu among his traded star path resources.",
        "chapters": [
          1343
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production-and-later-trade",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
